Text:
to verify access to high-risk systems remains commensurate with job 
responsibilities.  If any individual is identified to have inappropriate access, it is immediately remediated. 
  
Upon notification of an employee termination, an offboarding ticket is opened to initiate the process.  Termination 
date and last day worked is entered into the ticketing system among other details.  On the last day worked, the 
HRIS is automatically updated to show the employee is no longer active.  An automated job from SailPoint syncs 
with the HRIS, and any users newly marked as inactive are processed through the leaver job, which deactivates 
high-risk system access. 
  
In a separate process, ServiceNow employees who manage, and support customer instances of the Now Platform 
may be required to gain access to a customer instance of the Now Platform to address customer-specific support 
requests for a change, address a case or perform a customer-specified task in response to a change or case ticket.

